          "text": "Description: A witness observes the rapid and silent movement of two gray-silver balls. The characteristics described in the observation correspond to those known of balloons (metallic-looking balls moving silently, 'drifting with the wind' trajectories moving away from the witness). The observation was made on a Sunday in early afternoon (2:15 local time) in the direction of a heavily populated urban area. The case consistency is low (single witness, concise and poorly detailed observation report). The plausible hypothesis of balloons or other flying objects not being verified due to lack of information and the poor consistency of the case.",
